ull,"status":"open","entry":3850.0,"entry_t":"2026-10-28","exit":null,"exit_t":null,"reason":null,"sessions":13,"horizon":21,"stop":3399.3179844447545,"target":null,"r":null,"ret_pct":2.5,"excess_pct":null},{"book":"twin","symbol":"SUPREMEIND","direction":"down","signal_date":"2026-10-26","grade":"B","verdict":null,"conviction":null,"status":"open","entry":3247.813,"entry_t":"2026-10-27","exit":null,"exit_t":null,"reason":null,"sessions":14,"horizon":21,"stop":3541.7499651227677,"target":null,"r":null,"ret_pct":-0.6,"excess_pct":null}],"cases":[{"id":"NSE-mid-2026-11-16-ASALCBR.NS-down","market":"IN","horizon":"mid","symbol":"ASALCBR","name":null,"date":"2026-11-16","side":"short","grade":"B","headline":"Breakdown (shadow short) in a Weak market","stats":[["Grade","B"],["RS rank","3.0"],["Template","0/8"],["Base","15d"],["Volume","4.74x"],["Vs 50-day","-14.9%"],["From 52w high","-56.1%"],["3-month","-28.5%"]],"bull":"**Case for acting on the short signal (Bull = pro-signal), stated honestly.**\n\n**Trend and stage:** This is a textbook Stage 4 decline. The close of 517.75 sits 14.9% below the 50-day SMA and 31.8% below the 200-day. It is 56% off the 52-week high and 0.34% above the 52-week low, so it is at the low. Returns are negative at every horizon: 21d -12.0%, 63d -28.5%, 126d -38.9%, 252d -55.6%. The benchmark's 63-day return is +0.4%, so the stock is falling on its own, not with the market.\n\n**Relative strength:** The RS rank is 3 and the Mansfield reading is -35.84. That is near the bottom of the universe.\n\n**Volume and breakdown:** The signal bar is decisive. It opened at 558, made a low of 516, and closed at 517.75 on 157,911 shares. That is about 4.7x the volume ratio and the largest volume in the whole daily series, bar the 225k on 5/25. It closed at the low of the day, 8.6% below the prior close of 566.5. It also broke the 524 pivot, the 10/23 low, on heavy volume. The 11/2 to 11/12 bounce stalled at a 597.6 high, a lower high, which is consistent with supply.\n\n**Market context:** The regime is Weak, the benchmark is below a rising 200-day, and only 47.6% of stocks are in Stage 2. That backdrop is mildly supportive of a short.\n\n**Stop and target:** The screen's stop is 571.13, 10.3% above entry. That is a wide stop, about 2.5x ATR (ATR is 4.1%), and it sits above the 11/13 close of 566.5, so a recovery of the whole bounce would be needed to hit it. A 21-session target near 450 to 470 (a measured move from the 524 to 597 range) would give roughly 1.2 to 1.6R.\n\n**Honest weaknesses:** The track record is poor. For the same grade, n=361 gives avg R -0.29 and a 43% win rate. For same grade and regime, n=279 gives avg R -0.46 and a 38% win rate. The most similar cases (n=25) have a median R of 0.01 and a 52% win rate, which is too small to lean on. The stock is also extended after a 12% fall in 21 days, so a bounce is likely. Also, this is a delivery-only account, so an actual short may not be executable.\n\n**What would prove me wrong:** A close back above 566.5, or a reclaim of 524 on volume. Any close above 571.13 is a failed breakdown.","bear":"The short is a poor risk for a Rs 1 lakh delivery-only account, and the screen's own history says so.\n\n**Base rates.** Past shorts from this screen with the same grade lost money: n=361, average R -0.29, median -0.19, win rate 43%, average excess return -1.0%. In the same weak regime they did worse: n=279, average R -0.46, win rate 38%. The most similar cases (n=25) are a coin flip, with a 52% win rate and a median R of 0.01. That n is too small to lean on, and it still shows no edge. The screen's grades were also tuned on this history, so the real figures are probably worse.\n\n**Delivery-only.** The pack gives no way to short in delivery. Indian retail cannot hold a short for one to three months without futures, and this pack does not show whether any derivative exists on this stock. The signal may not be tradeable as written.\n\n**Extended and late.** The close of 517.75 is 56% below the 52-week high and 0.34% above the 52-week low. It is 31.8% under the SMA200 and 14.9% under the SMA50. The 252-day return is -55.6% and the 126-day return is -38.9%. Selling the low of a long decline invites a snapback. The stock bounced from 538 to 588 in early November, about 9%, before this drop.\n\n**Capitulation volume.** Volume on the signal day was 157,911, against a typical 15,000-50,000. The vol_ratio is 4.74. A 7% drop to a 52-week low on a volume spike often marks exhaustion rather than the start of a leg. The close sits near the low, which is bearish, but the entry is also the worst price in the move.\n\n**Stop and reward.** The stop is 571.13, 53.38 points or 10.3% above entry. That is wide against a 4.1% ATR. At 0.5% risk, the position is only about Rs 48,500 in notional. A 21-session hold needs a further drop of over 10% just to reach 1R, and one rebound day like 11 Nov (+3.5%) cuts into that.\n\n**What supports the short.** Stage 4, an RS rank of 3, a Mansfield of -35.8, a Weak regime and a benchmark below its SMA200 are all bearish. They are already priced into the screen's poor outcomes.\n\n**What would change my mind:** a failed bounce that stays under about 540, falling volume on the rebound, and confirmation that the short can actually be held for weeks.","judge":{"verdict":"Avoid","tone":"avoid","title":"Avoid","text":"The stock has been falling steadily for a year. It is down 55.6% over 252 days and now sits just 0.34% above its 52-week low and 31.8% below its 200-day average. It tried to bounce in early November, reaching 597.6, then broke under its 524 low on 16 Nov with a 7-9% drop on about 4.7 times normal volume, closing at the day's low. It is far weaker than the index, with a 63-day return of -28.5% against +0.4% for the benchmark and an RS rank of 3. No sector data is given.","conviction":4,"leverage":null,"reasons_for":["Clear Stage 4 decline: the close of 517.75 is 14.9% below the 50-day SMA and 31.8% below the 200-day, with negative returns at every horizon (21d -12.0%, 252d -55.6%).","Relative strength is near the bottom: RS rank 3 and Mansfield -35.84, while the benchmark gained 0.4% over 63 days.","The breakdown bar closed at its low (516 low, 517.75 close) and broke the 524 pivot on a 4.74x volume ratio, after a lower high of 597.6.","The market regime is Weak, the benchmark is not above a rising SMA200, and the Stage 2 share is only 47.6%."],"reasons_against":["The screen's own base rates are negative. Same grade: n=361, avg R -0.29, win rate 43%. Same grade and Weak regime: n=279, avg R -0.46, win rate 38%. Most-similar cases: n=25, median R 0.01, too small a sample and still no edge.","The account is delivery-only, so a 21-63 session short cannot be held in cash equity. The signal is not executable as written.","The entry is 0.34% above the 52-week low after a 28.5% fall in 63 days. A volume spike of 157,911 shares, against a typical 15-50k, can be capitulation that invites a snapback like the earlier 538 to 597.6 bounce.","The stop at 571.13 is 53.38 points (10.3%, about 2.5 ATR at a 4.12% ATR) above entry. A 1.5R target needs a further drop to about 435, roughly another 16%, within the holding window."],"invalidation":"The short case fails on any close above 571.13. A close back above 566.5 (the 11/13 close), with the 524 pivot reclaimed, would mark the breakdown as a failed capitulation.","wait":null,"wait_status":null,"horizon_sessions":21,"levels":{"entry_low":512.0,"entry_high":524.0,"stop":571.13,"target":435.0,"target_2":400.0}},"twin":{"levels":{"entry_low":517.75,"entry_high":517.75,"stop":571.13,"target":null}},"outcome":{"judge":{"status":"pending","entry":null,"entry_t":null,"exit":null,"exit_t":null,"reason":null,"r":null,"ret_pct":null,"excess_pct":null,"sessions":null,"stop":571.13,"target":435.0,"horizon":21},"judge_book":"debated","twin":{"status":"pending","entry":null,"entry_t":null,"exit":null,"exit_t":null,"reason":null,"r":null,"ret_pct"